WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.374 --> 00:00:03.941
- [Voiceover] This is the
Guatemalan Beaded Lizard.

00:00:03.941 --> 00:00:07.008
It's bite can be deadly, but
we're a larger threat to it

00:00:07.008 --> 00:00:08.425
than it is to us.

00:00:11.404 --> 00:00:14.157
There are less than 200 of these
creatures left in the wild,

00:00:14.157 --> 00:00:18.080
making it one of the most
endangered lizards in the world.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.651
Their beaded-like skin is adorned

00:00:19.651 --> 00:00:21.987
with yellow spots and bands.

00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:24.845
They can be found mainly
in deserts and dry forests,

00:00:24.845 --> 00:00:27.498
but even then their hard
to find as they spend

00:00:27.498 --> 00:00:31.171
about 70 percent of
their lives underground.

00:00:31.171 --> 00:00:33.480
Measuring up to a foot and
a half when fully grown,

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.577
they can pack a serious punch.

00:00:36.577 --> 00:00:39.702
They are one of only two lizard
species that are venomous.

00:00:39.702 --> 00:00:42.250
The venom is in their
saliva and it's administered

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.950
when they bite their prey.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:48.684
Unfortunately, this venom also
strikes fear among humans,

00:00:48.684 --> 00:00:53.040
the biggest threat to these
otherwise docile creatures.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.917
Hunting habitat loss and poaching have

00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:59.525
forced this phantom lizard
to fight for its survival.

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:02.608
This is the Guatemalan Beaded Lizard.

